    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "process Process_Ingestion",
      "prov:value": "The document pipeline that used to be this diagram's body (rungs, the four ingest phases, the L1 completeness gate, promotion, the summary queue) is such a refinement now, in the layer above."
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "lane Lane_1",
      "prov:value": "It asks one question — is the asset materialized? — and that is answered from the materialization state vocabulary (`schemas/kg/materialization-state.ts`, placement PR5), not by judgement.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "placement PR5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "startEvent StartEvent_Dropped",
      "prov:value": "ONE OF TWO ENTRY POINTS, and this said \"the only\" one until 2026-09-20. A drop during an editing session triggers ingestion in the background; the contributor does not wait for it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "startEvent StartEvent_Dropped",
      "prov:value": "RENAMED 2026-09-30, and the id is deliberately unchanged. This event was named \"A file lands in uploads/\" — an ARRIVAL, which is why the owner could say the chain's first link was missing: the process began after the file was already in the queue, so nothing in it modelled, governed or documented how the file got there. Task_Place is that step, and an event named for the arrival could not sit in front of it without contradicting it. The id stays `StartEvent_Dropped` because it is referenced from `library/skills/library-core/content-acquisition.md` and from five translation catalogues, and an id is an identifier rather than a description.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "task Task_Place",
      "prov:value": "The routes, what each writer owes, and the two that are mechanisms against the one that is a persona are in the `upload-routes` skill; `upload-url` composes the forge URL for the web route from the declaration rather than from a literal, because a hand-written one 404'd."
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "task Task_Place",
      "prov:value": "What it owes the work plan is visibility — three batches of PDFs arrived through the forge's web UI (`c8349950fa5`, `f4ddfc65c8d`, `b8549160bb1`) with no bean, no PR and no note, and the first sibling to notice was a generator going stale. A note against the ingestion bean is what makes the queue's growth something another session can see."
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "serviceTask Task_ExtractMetadata",
      "prov:value": "What enters the knowledge graph is the asset's INDEX — what it is, how big, what type, when it says it was written — and, for a container, what is in it; its contents do not go in unless somebody asks, with a reason. Owner, 2026-09-20: \"make sure you have zip ingestion skills to extract metadata of assets into KG. don't extract contents unless explict ask by user.\" The tool is `cat-harness-tools/scripts/extract-assets.ts`, writing a `folio-extraction/v1` record (`schemas/content/extraction.ts`, moved down to this layer in placement PR5).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "placement PR5"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "serviceTask Task_PlaceInLibrary",
      "prov:value": "The upload is then RETIRED, not left and not deleted: it moves to fsh-guts/uploads/ beside a sidecar naming where it came from and when (owner, 2026-09-29), and `check:uploads-retired` finds one that was not.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "process Process_Ingestion",
      "prov:value": "REWRITTEN AS THE BASIC FLOW in placement PR6 (bean `apcg`; owner ruling 3, 2026-09-30): \"only basic doc ingestion high level workflow in cat-harness. very little process context assumed. just that the uploaded asset has extracted metadata inserted into KG and asset in library/ (if materialized).\" Accept, extract the metadata into the KG, ask whether the asset is materialized, place it in library/&lt;slug&gt;/.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean apcg",
        "2026-09-30",
        "placement PR6"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "lane Lane_0",
      "prov:value": "UNDOCUMENTED UNTIL 2026-09-30, and legitimately so until then: the lane held nothing but a start event, and a lane with no activity has no performer to describe. Task_Place gave it one.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "lane Lane_0",
      "prov:value": "\"HUMAN OR AGENT\" IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A HEDGE. Over this repository's own history both have stood here: files have reached a queue in commits authored by `Carl Leitner` (including 16 made through the forge's web form, committer `GitHub`) and in commits authored by `Claude`. That is why Task_Place is a plain `bpmn:task` rather than a `userTask` — asserting a human performs it would contradict the lane's own role graph, which is what `activity-fulfilment-kind` exists to catch."
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "startEvent StartEvent_Dropped",
      "prov:value": "THE OTHER is materialization: an asset listed in a remote graph that this instance, or one of its dependencies, declares in `remoteGraphs`. Owner, 2026-09-20: \"things can enter library through uploads/ -&gt; library/ document ingestion or through retrieval / materialization of asset known through listed external KG in one of the dependent harnesses.\"",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "task Task_Place",
      "prov:value": "THE FIRST LINK, and it did not exist until 2026-09-30. Everything downstream of here takes a file that is already in the queue, and both ingest Tools type their first input as \"The upload to ingest, under the declared `uploads` graph\". So the act of PUTTING it there was performed by three different mechanisms and governed by none of them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
